This project ports StockBench to the Inspect evaluation framework.

StockBench: Can LLM Agents Trade Stocks Profitably In Real-world Markets?
https://github.com/ChenYXxxx/stockbench
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The files in src/stockbench_inspect/prompts/ are copied unchanged from
stockbench/agents/prompts/ at commit ce8b2b3483590646ad3b650ac8221f43f76fd091.
The trading engine, agent loop and metrics are reimplemented from the same commit.
This repository contains no price, news, fundamentals or dividend files. When the eval
first runs, it downloads the StockBench repository archive at the same commit from GitHub,
keeps the files listed in src/stockbench_inspect/data/SHA256SUMS and checks each file's hash.
The StockBench README says its data comes from Polygon and Finnhub. That data stays under the
terms that apply to it upstream, and this project grants no rights to it.
